# Patterns to ignore when building packages (helm package / helm
# dependency update). Unlike .gitignore, this controls what gets bundled
# into the .tgz a downstream consumer pulls in via file:// (or a real
# chart repo, once published) — so it matters for more than repo
# hygiene: without excluding harness/ here, every downstream `helm
# dependency update` would repackage my-crd's ENTIRE directory tree,
# including harness/'s own charts/my-crd-0.0.0.tgz (its bundled copy of
# my-crd, from testing the harness locally) — which itself may contain
# a stale, even-earlier-nested copy, growing with every local test
# cycle. This exact recursive bloat hit crdkit for real once (pushed a
# packaged .tgz past 5MB and broke helm-unittest's file-size limit) —
# added here preventively before my-crd has any downstream consumer of
# its own. harness/ and tests/ are my-crd's own local dev/test
# scaffolding — a downstream consumer never needs either.
harness/
tests/

# Generated documentation (make docs): for readers and editors, never
# read by a render.
input.schema.json
VALUES.html
VALUES.md

# Common VCS dirs
.git/
.gitignore
.helmignore

# Common backup files
*.swp
*.bak
*.tmp
*.orig

# Various IDEs
.project
.idea/
*.tmproj
.vscode/
.DS_Store
